"pull" prints a command's output only if the command fails.  The program makes the file and
directory names absolute, and adds the directory to the "update aborted" message.

The replacer for "cvs update: conflicts found in FILE" requires two spaces before the file name,
so it does not apply to this message, and the file name remains relative.  The file name in the
"C" line also remains relative, because no replacer handles that line.  The goal file records the
current (wrong) behavior.

Bug report: https://github.com/plume-lib/multi-version-control/issues/616
